From 45f5061a3009f4bf16adb3dce84bc868d9cecdf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(spofy-subpage): serialize checkout per user

The bot keeps one «current cart» slot per user, so two parallel checkout
POSTs (two tabs) overwrote each other's cart and bind_cart_to_payment:
the first payment stopped matching its cart (is_funded_by_payment) and
the money hung on the balance without a purchase.

Checkout is now serialized per user (asyncio, one slot per user id):
* the first request claims the slot and runs the whole critical section
  to completion — clear slot, save cart, create payment, bind cart;
* a parallel request with the SAME cart + method waits for the first one
  and replays the same payment (idempotency anchor = payment_id, replay
  window 30 minutes), so two tabs never create two payments for the one
  cart;
* a parallel request with a DIFFERENT cart gets 409 right away — letting
  it wait and then overwrite the slot mid-checkout is exactly the broken
  state this prevents; it can be retried once the first payment exists.

Applies on top of the current bot main (patches 0001-0004 are already
merged there).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
